nav-starter = Starter
starter-title = Starter feeding calculator
starter-description = When a refreshed starter will peak, which feeding ratio peaks at the time you want, and what to weigh for a levain build.
starter-lead = A starter peaks when its microbes have grown back to the density of a ripe starter. The more fresh flour per part of starter, and the cooler the kitchen, the longer it takes.
starter-solve-time = When will it peak, with this feed
starter-solve-ratio = Which feed peaks at this time
starter-target = Hours from feeding to peak
starter-feed = Feed (starter : flour : water)
starter-flour-parts = Fresh flour per part of starter
starter-parts-hint = 5 for a 1:5:5 feed.
starter-water-parts = Fresh water per part of starter
starter-hyd-target = Hydration of the refreshed starter
starter-hyd-target-hint = 100 % for a liquid starter, 50–60 % for a stiff one.
starter-seed-hyd = Hydration of the starter you feed
starter-temp = Temperature of the starter
starter-temp-hint = Where the jar sits; a small jar takes the room temperature quickly.
starter-need = Refreshed starter wanted
starter-need-hint = Optional: the grams of seed, flour and water to weigh.
starter-peak-result = Peaks about { $t } after feeding
starter-ratio-result = Feed { $ratio }
starter-range = Likely between { $low } and { $high } (80 % of feeds); your own starter can be up to three times faster or slower.
starter-hydration = Hydration
starter-seed-share = Seed's share of the flour
starter-build = To weigh
starter-build-seed = Starter (seed)
starter-note-too-fast = No feed peaks that fast at this temperature: shown, the richest feed (1 : 0.2). Warm the starter or allow more time.
starter-note-too-slow = Even a very thin feed peaks sooner than that: shown, the thinnest feed (1 : 100). Use a cooler place or the fridge.
starter-how = The starter grows from its seed share of the flour back to ripe density at a rate set by temperature, the curve measured by Gänzle and colleagues (1998), and by the starter's hydration (stiff starters are slower). Calibrated on published peak times; a starter's vigour varies from kitchen to kitchen, hence the wide range.
